  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "How this pattern applies to all fourteen workflows",
      "items": [
        "Each W01\u2013W14 has its own trigger and minimum completion evidence in the companion connection map. This flowchart is the shared proposed control pattern, not an already running job scheduler.",
        "W01/W02/W06/W09/W10/W11 often prepare a finding, follow-up or checklist rather than mutate ShiftCare; the read/review-only branch keeps that distinction.",
        "For W03/W04/W07/W08/W12, select only a supported, exactly reviewed action. W05 files natively. W13 needs verified delivery or a recorded human contact; W14 uses a separate consented journey.",
        "Engine execution and sending remain fictional in the prototype. Trial MCP proof establishes only the specifically approved administrative action and its separate read-back."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Triggers and data entering the shared controls",
      "items": [
        "W01 new enquiry; W02 authorised message; W03 accepted intake/profile correction; W04 employee form; W05 returned agreement/file.",
        "W06 native reminder reply/silence; W07 matched cancellation; W08 booking/change/sickness/decline/cover deadline.",
        "W09 native visit evidence update; W10 agreed Tuesday cut-off; W11 agreed pay-period cut-off; W12 cleanup/expiry/new evidence.",
        "W13 verified outcome/feedback/announcement; W14 current assignment plus assigned-worker consent and journey start.",
        "Retain account, source ID/time, permitted person/shift/assignment IDs, local period/time zone, original evidence and scope completeness. Do not convert absent fields into confirmed facts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Approval and method selection",
      "items": [
        "Office/intake/HR/bookkeeper reviews fields and the original, then exact target, scope, consent, reason and financial consequence where relevant.",
        "W07: whole-shift with-charge cancellation cannot be used for one participant in a group; missing policy or financial lock requires native review.",
        "W08: reviewed availability/suitability and native worker acceptance precede final assignment. Assignment arrays preserve all unaffected people; occurrence/series changes differ.",
        "Unsupported upload, staff edit, message sending, worker acceptance or pricing configuration becomes a native task, not an invented API call.",
        "Re-read current native context before dispatch; changed meaning invalidates approval. MCP tool exposure is not a REST write contract."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Independent result and workflow-specific completion",
      "items": [
        "Native action: returned remote ID and independently checked expected fields; original write response alone cannot prove completion.",
        "W03/W04: profile plus separate accounting/payroll linking evidence. W05/W12: original evidence and checked native filing/metadata; never infer never-expires from a blank date.",
        "W08 offer and final assignment are separate verified steps around native worker acceptance; no cover remains an owned exception.",
        "W09/W10/W11: complete permitted source, reviewed exceptions and checked native finance/export/payroll references. No automatic clinical decision or pay release.",
        "W13: own delivery/contact evidence. W14: permitted current booking, active consent and fresh journey data; arrival is not attendance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Failure routes and expected outcome",
      "items": [
        "Unclear match, incomplete read or missing prerequisites \u2192 clarify/re-review with the named owner; no guessed ID, charge or availability.",
        "Permission/feature/connector unavailable \u2192 owned native action; preserve the request and show the blocked method.",
        "Unknown write response \u2192 reconciliation. Search/read the target before any further dispatch; when context changes, return to fresh exact approval.",
        "Read-back mismatch \u2192 verification pending and admin reconciliation; never mark completed merely because the queue or demo reports success.",
        "No acceptance/cover, document uncertainty or accounting mismatch \u2192 appropriate human handoff and an explicit outcome, not a silent terminal success.",
        "Delivery failure \u2192 bounded message retry or agreed contact fallback. It never reruns a cancellation, profile creation or assignment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Data ownership and audit trail",
      "items": [
        "ShiftCare owns people, roster, original care/docs and service billing. Existing accounting/payroll systems retain financial release.",
        "OCD owns source references, matching/proposals, job state, approvals, owned exceptions and sanitized operation/delivery receipts.",
        "Use stable source/operation/target keys and durable job claims in production; app-level deduplication does not prove upstream idempotency.",
        "Record approver, account/record IDs, allowed changes, source/read-back times, result, owner and next action. Protect clinical contents and server credentials."
      ]
    }
  ],
